  "Question": "What is the sum of the prime factors of \\(2010?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( \\ 67 \\)",
    "B": "\\( \\ 75 \\)",
    "C": "\\( \\ 77 \\)",
    "D": "\\( \\ 201 \\)",
    "E": "\\( \\ 210 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The final zero suggests separating a factor of \\(10\\):\n\\[\n2010=201\\cdot10\n=(3\\cdot67)(2\\cdot5)\n=2\\cdot3\\cdot5\\cdot67.\n\\]\nTo confirm that the factorization is complete, check \\(67\\). If it were composite, a factor pair would have a smaller factor below \\(9\\), since \\(9\\cdot9>67\\). It would therefore have a prime divisor among \\(2,3,5,7\\), but none divides \\(67\\). Thus \\(67\\) is prime.\n\nThe required sum is\n\\[\n2+3+5+67=\\boxed{77},\n\\]\nchoice C.",
